Z||000000||penetrator||02-25-2000||06:58 AM||||Is the bhp bench horse power or back wheel Hp's ? Or whats Bhp ?<P><BR>Thanks<BR>Magnus||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||02-25-2000||08:06 AM||||bhp= brake horsepower<P>I just found this link for you. Should answer any questions. <A HREF="http://www.fwkc.com/encyclopedia/low/articles/h/h011001344f.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fwkc.com/encyclopedia/low/articles/h/h011001344f.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 02-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||02-25-2000||08:52 AM||||Hp can be measured at either the flywheel or the rear wheels. There is about a 20% difference between the two, rear wheel HP is lower because it shows the power loss going through the drivetrain. Most manufacturers quote flywheel numbers(looks better in the ads).||||reg||1
Z||000003||penetrator||02-25-2000||09:43 AM||||Thanks for the answers. :-)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||02-25-2000||09:37 PM||||Car manufacturers have not used flywheel numbers in years, I believe since insurance companies pitched the fits in the early 70's. The camaro rated at 300 HP is supposed to be 300 HP at the wheels. A few years ago, a friend was trying to set the land speed record for a stock displacement production vehicle with a twin turbo RX7. He tested MANY of these cars on a chasis dyno. They were rated at 300 HP, but none that he dynoed came in at less than 320 at the wheels. BTW, after he juiced the new RX7 with aftermarket add ons, the local dealership quickly cancelled his warrenty! ||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||02-25-2000||11:52 PM||||Everyone but Ford, sorry for the f word... Is usually close to thier mark on HP/TQ number. There is a class action suit comming together now that a local speed shop is in on.. the new Cobras are Rated at like 320hp we'll they barly lay down 260.. and as for the 1/4 times.. the manufactures claiming mid 13s.. not very many will even come close to 14 flat...  R&T drivers were the first to notice this and then once the owners realized they got nailed on the price and still have a POS they got upset. (Inorder to be in this suit you MUST have your car Dynoed and have a all the atmospheric conditions written down in addition to the Techs name address phone # and ASE certs, model of dyno used) They are not asking for  for money but just to have the better motor. (which many result in head upgrades for everyone involved) just a fun fact... useless cannon fodder thats all... not sure where you can get more info on this topic but i got it from <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>    ||||reg||1
